00:12:46.791 --> 00:12:52.890
Okay, so volumes and surface
areas are just integrals.

00:12:52.891 --> 00:12:54.310
And so
we can work them out in 3-d,

00:12:54.311 --> 00:12:57.250
we can also work them out in
any number of dimensions.

00:12:57.251 --> 00:12:59.910
So 3-d is multiple integration,
three integrals.

00:12:59.911 --> 00:13:02.830
Instead you'll have D
integrals now, right?

00:13:02.831 --> 00:13:04.870
Now here are some simple facts,
right?

00:13:04.871 --> 00:13:09.720
The volume for cube of side 1
in three dimensions is still 1,

00:13:09.721 --> 00:13:10.289
okay?

00:13:10.290 --> 00:13:11.895
That's good.

00:13:11.896 --> 00:13:14.430
This is the cube, right?

00:13:14.431 --> 00:13:15.880
So the volume is 1.

00:13:15.881 --> 00:13:19.240
What's the volume of
a cube of side 2?

00:13:19.241 --> 00:13:20.783
So if they scale each side by 2,

00:13:20.784 --> 00:13:23.472
in three dimensions you scale
the volume by 8, right,

00:13:23.473 --> 00:13:26.710
in two dimensions by 4, in three
dimensions by 8 and so on.

00:13:26.711 --> 00:13:28.530
In D dimensions you scale
it up by 2 to the d.

00:13:30.040 --> 00:13:32.310
Cuz every dimension
scales up by 2.

00:13:32.311 --> 00:13:35.203
Good thing to remember.

00:13:35.204 --> 00:13:36.850
What about the d
dimensional sphere?

00:13:36.851 --> 00:13:40.120
Also the same, if I up
the radius by a factor of 2,

00:13:40.121 --> 00:13:43.000
I up the volume by
a factor of 2 to the d.

00:13:43.001 --> 00:13:47.430
Okay, these all follows by
